      "content": "Taking additional iron without medical advice can still lead to serious risks, including iron overload, which can cause organ damage. The body's ability to process iron supplements should be carefully monitored and managed by a healthcare provider for safe treatment. In the meantime, you might consider other supportive measures that can help alleviate some of your son's tiredness, such as a balanced diet with foods rich in iron and possibly discussing vitamin C-rich foods that enhance iron absorption with your son's healthcare team when they can be seen. It's essential to prioritize safety and communication with the medical professional overseeing his care.",
